  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ae309fc9b93c4434b888290b1d747f9a, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TeacherInteraction
  playerMovement: {fileID: 916875898}
  teacherName: Brodeur
  dialoguePopUp: {fileID: 208243415}
  dialogueManager: {fileID: 1165950374}
  spellSelectionScreen: {fileID: 0}
  element: 
  totalNumOfElementSpells: 0
  initalLines:
  - Hey! Do you want to see something cool?
  - "You\u2019re here to learn about poison magic, so the fundamentals are obviously
    that in many cases, it\u2019s dangerous to have contact with eyes and skin."
  - But if you carefully manipulate it like this, it can be very useful, especially
    if mixed.
  - Give it a try yourself. The instructions are scattered around the room.
  afterPuzzleLines:
  - Combined with this, to work with poison, you have to both build a resistance
    and learn how to contain it.
  - Show me what you know, then.
  afterBattleLines:
  - "I think you\u2019re just about ready."
  afterSpellLines:
  - 'One more note! '
  - Poison magic seems to be totally nullified by Obsidian.
  - "Don\u2019t be complacent, but I think it might really come in handy as a tool
    for accidental spills."
